ize those uh as um regions as as  uh legitimized legitimately recognize  those areas as independent so putin is  saying okay it's part of ukraine  donetsk is part of ukraine luhansk is  part of ukraine but there are  separatists there who quote really are  russian they speak the language they  want to be part of russia so we're going  to say those are independent regions not  ukrainian regions now if you're ukraine  you say wait hold on  it's it's part of the country it's  ukraine but putin says no those are  those are independent regions  he then hours later after some mild  sanctions were imposed by the eu and the  united states on uh on putin for doing  this hours later and really the  sanctions were imposed on those regions  rather than on what we might consider  russia proper putin says hey  are the separatists in those quote  independent areas that i've recognized  they are going they're under attack so  we need to go in and send in  peacekeeping forces into that area it's  the putin playbook hook line and sinker  and there shouldn't really be anything  surprising about it  this is what he was signaling for a long  time this is what various foreign policy  analysts and experts were saying could  could be done for a long time some kind  of pretext to then send in troops but  you know they call them peacekeeping but  it doesn't matter how slow it is it  doesn't matter if you say you're there  to keep the peace it is still  fundamentally  an invasion we have video  um where you see  um  tanks rolling down the road this was  yesterday shortly after this  announcement was made  and of course the question now is to  what degree is this going to escalate or  grow now there are some people who we'll  talk about in a little bit  who are really going out of their way to  sort of defend and normalize what russia  is doing and you can be against american  involvement and be against war and be  against violence the way that i am  and still recognize that this is a  classic russian playbook that this is an  invasion that russia has no right to  send tanks uh where they are sending  tanks into the donetsk and luhansk  regions and just imagine a similar  situation with mexico or quebec these  are not perfect analogies but imagine  that mexico said hey you know what  um there are people in texas and arizona  they look like us  and they speak spanish our language and  they would prefer  to be part of mexico  rather than the united states in texas  or arizona so we are recognizing these  enclaves of mexican-americans as mexico  they are independent as far as mexico is  concerned well in the u.s we would say  yeah but that's the united states and i  mean they could go to mexico you're not  stopping if you want to welcome them  they could go and then mexico says well  listen on the basis of the independence  of these uh separatists we're gonna send  some peacekeeping troops in come on guys  nobody would go for it think of quebec  another analogy these are not perfect  analogies but they they are useful in  thinking about this  in quebec there is a separate this  movement imagine that that separatist  movement in quebec canada said well we  don't want to be our own country  we want to be part of the united states  would would the u.s have any right to  say hey those quebec separatists we  think of them as independent because  they really want to be part of us oh  they need us to help keep them safe  we're going to send some tanks there  give me a break guys it's absolutely  absurd now we have video from the eu  foreign policy chief joseph burrell  who is still kind of hedging a little  bit as to the terms that are being used  let's take a listen  well the russian troops has entered in  donbass  we consider donbass part of ukraine  so certainly the russian troops entered  into the donbas ukrainian  i wouldn't say that a fully fledged  invasion  but russian troops are on the ukrainian  side yeah they've invaded one part of  russia is what we i'm sorry one part of  ukraine  um the idea  maybe just do this and then back off  we don't know and again i hope that  people recognize that all along i've  said  we can make assessments based on the  signals but we don't really know what  putin plans to do this could just be one  tiny step a day so there's never any one  day where it's like wow look at what  happened and then they moved towards  kiev  um  it's just it's not completely clear  um  we are also going to have to consider  what putin's greater ideology here is  and it's sort of like the idea of  pointing back to the former ussr  ukraine is really important in putin's  mind in kind of recreating that and  we'll talk about that on the bonus show  today but also in terms of tactics this  is really kind of back to like an old  war concept which is can you just change  your country's borders by force since  world war ii  and since the codification  in international law that prohibits the  threat or use of force against  territorial integrity or political  independence we've seen few attempts to  just change your country's border by  force in this degree now you could say  well you know there's a bunch of areas  of the border  in india where there are constant  disputes and small skirmishes and little  bits of land taken and given back and it  is changing the border in a way by force  in in major ways there have really only  been four attempts since world war ii  north korea in 1950 trying to conquer  south korea  north vietnam successfully conquering  south vietnam in 75  indonesia uh annexing t more less than  75 and that very short very short-lived  iraqi annexation of kuwait in 1990  before it was liberated in what we call  the first gulf war so  this is not super common since world war  ii it will be important not only to  watch what happens in russia but also to  watch china's behavior and ambitions on  the basis of what happens with russia  ukraine because if russia gets away with  this  china's interest in similar action with  taiwan may increase so a lot at play  here and in the immediate it's going to  remain extraordinarily chaotic  one of our sponsors is nebia who's  introducing their newest shower head the  nebia by moan cuatro  it was designed by former nasa engineers  who spent years researching how to save  water quattro is the world's best high  pressure water saving showerhead  starting at just 119  and quattro uses 40 to 50 percent less  water than traditional shower heads  helping the planet helping your wallet  still giving you the high pressure water  stream you love with four different  spray modes literally takes one to two  minutes to install easy as screwing in a  light bulb i love it i have the rain  shower version i've been using nebia  shower heads for a while now i love  saving the water and i love the high  pressure spray it's really the best of  both worlds nebia the maker of quattro  also offers sustainable bathroom  accessories i have the soft gray bath  mat and the nebia double shelf the  quattro showerhead is just 119 but nebia  is giving you ten percent off when you  go to nebia.com  pacman and use the promo code pacman the  link is underneath this video

